<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16961" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exortīvus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		2. exortus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to the
			rising</i> of the heavenly bodies, <i>ascendant</i>
			(post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mensura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 49, 50, § 160</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>towards the
			sunrise</i>, <i>eastern</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pars,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 34, 77, § 338</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oceanus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					37, 2, 11, § 39</span></i>
			.—In the <i>neutr. plur. subst.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Narbonensis Galliae exortiva,</span>”
				<i>the eastern part</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					6, 34, 39, § 215</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
